a **multicast address** is a special IP address used for **one-to-many communication**—sending data from one source to multiple specific recipients simultaneously, without bothering everyone else on the network.

**IPv4 Multicast Range (Class D):**

- **Unicast**: One-to-one (like a phone call)
- **Broadcast**: One-to-all (like shouting in a room, blocked by routers)
- **Multicast**: One-to-group (like a conference call with specific participants)
